  "accepted_contract": {
    "canonical_authority": "Existing normal and sample lease functions share one reserved private delivery_state key; no new table/queue/store. Existing canonical writer remains byte-identical.",
    "accounting": "Maximum3 actual leased rows per run and864 shared new admissions per UTC day. Counts committed leased attempts, never successful extractions, approved briefs or finished homes; no refunds. Migration-day total is POST-ACTIVATION admissions only, excluding unknown earlier legacy attempts.",
    "single_flight": "Operational row lock before listing locks; post-lock clock and validation. Minimum15-minute run flight, up to60 for longer requested listing leases. Active prior-day run/bootstrap survives rollover. Matching known completion releases only its flight; stale/idempotent release cannot reset successor or budget. Unknown/aborted responses retain charged flight until expiry.",
    "bootstrap": "Default60-minute bootstrap blocks normal/sample/direct admission. Even exact-ID service release refuses. Root-only optional withdrawal is separately reviewed exact-CAS operation after actual quiescence/drain/new-worker/no-active-lease proof. No generic early-release RPC exists.",
    "database_safety": "Explicit atomic migrations, postgres ownership, empty search paths, private helper ACLs, service-only release, finite PG16/17 table ACL compatibility and exact actual function/table/column guards. Source writer untouched.",
    "dashboard": "Only a four-key predicate on existing feed aggregation; independent exact body reversal plus complete before/after JSON equality. Private operational row is excluded without changing ordinary founder data.",
    "schedule": "Separate activation requires paused original job30 with exact hourly identity/560-byte command hash, untouched disabled job10, no competing active enrichment job, six exact installed function/ACL/config/owner contracts and valid state. Same IDs/commands preserved, only job30 cadence/active change."
  },
